    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d340">

                <pb facs="0404" n="320" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg320"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 102.62/50</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Department of State to the Swiss Legation </hi>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The Department of State returns, herewith, the patent documents received with the
                    memorandum of the Legation of Switzerland (X–c–19), Department of German
                    Interests, dated May 9, 1917,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d340-f1"/> and states that
                    because of the state of war existing between the United States and Germany, the
                    Department cannot transmit to the Commissioner of Patents papers relating to the
                    patent applications of German subjects.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-18"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">May 18, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
